{"name":"Distance","hex":"#566a73","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"distance","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["An amount of space between points (often geographical points), usually (but not necessarily) measured along a straight line.","An amount of space between points (often geographical points), usually (but not necessarily) measured along a straight line."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["Often followed by from: to set (someone or something) at a distance (noun sense 1.1) from someone or something else.\n\nTo cause (a place, a thing, etc.) to seem distant, or  unfamiliar.\n\nTo leave behind (someone or something moving in the same direction; specifically, other competitors in a race) some distance away; to outpace, to outstrip.","Often followed by from: to set (someone or something) at a distance (noun sense 1.1) from someone or something else."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/distance"}],"entries":[{"title":"Distance","blocks":[{"text":"Distance is a numerical or occasionally qualitative measurement of how far apart objects, points, people, or ideas are. In physics or everyday usage, distance may refer to a physical length or an estimation based on other criteria. The term is also frequently used metaphorically to mean a measurement of the amount of difference between two similar objects or a degree of separation. Most such notions of distance, both physical and metaphorical, are formalized in mathematics using the notion of a metric space."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/9d/Distance_board_in_Vizag_cropped.jpg/330px-Distance_board_in_Vizag_cropped.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Distance","wikidata":"Q126017"},{"title":"Distance (Hikaru Utada album)","blocks":[{"text":"Distance is the third studio album by Japanese-American singer Hikaru Utada. Toshiba EMI released it on March 28, 2001, making it their second release with the label. Utada wrote and co-produced the majority of the album, alongside previous collaborators Akira Miyake and Teruzane Utada, as well as new collaborations with American producers Rodney Jerkins and Jimmy Jam & Terry Lewis. Distance, like its predecessor First Love (1999), is influenced by pop music and R&B, with additional hip-hop, rock, reggae, and techno influences from Western music."}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/1/14/Utadadistance.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Distance_(Hikaru_Utada_album)","wikidata":"Q2699535"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/fe/Distance_function_animation.gif/500px-Distance_function_animation.gif?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/fe/Distance_function_animation.gif/500px-Distance_function_animation.gif?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Animation visualizing the function \n  \n    \n      \n        (\n        \n          |\n        \n        x\n        \n          \n            |\n          \n          \n            r\n          \n        \n        +\n        \n          |\n        \n        y\n        \n          \n            |\n          \n          \n            r\n          \n        \n        \n          )\n          \n            1\n            \n              /\n            \n            r\n          \n        \n      \n    \n    {\\displaystyle (|x|^{r}+|y|^{r})^{1/r}}\n  \n for various values of r.","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ADistance_function_animation.gif"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/50/Ayumi_Hamasaki_2007.jpg/500px-Ayumi_Hamasaki_2007.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/50/Ayumi_Hamasaki_2007.jpg/500px-Ayumi_Hamasaki_2007.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Distance was released alongside A Best by Japanese singer Ayumi Hamasaki (pictured), which generated huge significance in Japanese and Western music media.","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AAyumi_Hamasaki_2007.jpg"}],"sounds":{"distance":[{"type":"audio/ogg; codecs=\"vorbis\"","src":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/2/2d/En-us-distance.ogg?utm_source=en.wiktionary.org&utm_campaign=rest&utm_content=original"},{"type":"audio/mpeg","src":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/transcoded/2/2d/En-us-distance.ogg/En-us-distance.ogg.mp3"},{"type":"audio/wav","src":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/b/bc/LL-Q1860_%28eng%29-Vealhurl-distance.wav?utm_source=en.wiktionary.org&utm_campaign=rest&utm_content=original"},{"type":"audio/mpeg","src":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/transcoded/b/bc/LL-Q1860_%28eng%29-Vealhurl-distance.wav/LL-Q1860_%28eng%29-Vealhurl-distance.wav.mp3"},{"type":"audio/ogg; codecs=\"vorbis\"","src":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/transcoded/b/bc/LL-Q1860_%28eng%29-Vealhurl-distance.wav/LL-Q1860_%28eng%29-Vealhurl-distance.wav.ogg"}]},"pictures":[{"title":"The Indian grey mongoose (Urva edwardsii) mating 4","image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/ca/The_Indian_grey_mongoose_%28Urva_edwardsii%29_mating_4.jpg/500px-The_Indian_grey_mongoose_%28Urva_edwardsii%29_mating_4.jpg","ratio":1.5,"link":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:The_Indian_grey_mongoose_(Urva_edwardsii)_mating_4.jpg","share":0.310625},{"title":"Grey rectangle","image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/0f/Grey_rectangle.jpg/500px-Grey_rectangle.jpg","ratio":0.75,"link":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Grey_rectangle.jpg","share":0.26875},{"title":"Al Grey (Gottlieb)","image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org